            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The base can last for decades if it drains well and is not overloaded. The surface is never permanent: stone migrates and wears, so most driveways need a top-up every two to five years and regrading once or twice a year. Think of gravel as a driveway you maintain continuously rather than replace on a schedule."
