            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On firm, well-drained soil, many driveways do fine without it. On soft clay or wet ground, a woven geotextile stabilization fabric is worth the modest cost because it keeps base stone from sinking into the soil. Thin landscape fabric for weeds is a different product and will not stabilize a driveway."
          }
